@cc [owner:fontanierh,label:correctness] reused-geometry-requires-current-finishing
Geometry reuse MUST still apply and verify the current owner's material, role, collision and LOD settings.
An already-equal source-LOD binding MUST NOT be dirtied solely to reassign it; clean source packages MUST
use dirty-only saves. Target assembly and its required current validation/saves MUST remain intact.
Geometry reuse alone MUST NOT be reported as unchanged package bytes, an avoided cook or whole-build success.

@cc [owner:fontanierh,label:correctness] native-source-proof-uses-real-import-data
Native source-MD5 admission MUST read the engine's actual AssetImportData registry evidence and validate
its supported shape and current source digest. Missing/malformed readback or a changed source MUST miss.
An obsolete tag name, a path match, serialized-string search or a staged package's presence MUST NOT
substitute for the required current loaded-source and native validation proof.

@cc [owner:fontanierh,label:correctness] partial-preparation-needs-current-owner-proof
A saved geometry-unit hint MAY survive parent failure but MUST NOT certify that parent or its registry.
A unit hit MUST prove current expected geometry-role closure, compiled preparation policy, complete
package bytes, native snapshot and current material/settings/source bindings. Missing hints MAY be
bootstrapped only through the same fresh expected-geometry and native checks, never by accepting a
package's existence or disabling a validator. Normal preparation MUST validate the complete current
roster and publish its registry only after every required unit and owner check succeeds.

@cc [owner:fontanierh,label:correctness;performance] fbx-source-only-bootstrap
Shared legacy FBX import MUST use the actual requested source for any Interchange-to-FBX
migration pass, then synchronize stored unit/normal/colour settings before the final pass.
An unrelated generated seed/placeholder MUST NOT enter final-source identity, be read or supply
material slots. Raw source-pass code and current validation MUST have distinct declared policies.
Source changes, real import-option changes, package-byte changes and failed native checks MUST
continue to refuse reuse. Obsolete seed keywords MAY remain accepted only without reading them.
